//@version=6
// SNM+ 3.49 — André Wonou; 3.47 baseline plus optional CISD Model+ integration
// Simple by design: it draws setups, it does not trade. ManipulationX core (liquidity sweep + iFVG + V-shape),
// intraday swings and equal highs / lows (EQH / EQL) as sweep levels and draws. Judas tag (J) at the NY open.
// iFVG on 1m / 2m / 3m / 5m: the highest timeframe inversion in the leg is preferred. each iFVG box is tagged, hover for its details.
// model tags: C continuation (edging a key level), RB rebalance (5m / 15m FVG), RV reversal (HTF draw), from the 15m structure; a reversal outside NY AM is flagged (Asia / London = continuation only).
// news blackout: NFP automatic (first Friday 08:30 NY), other releases typed by hand; setups inside are greyed and tagged NEWS.
// HRL: a high / low made by a sweep is protected; skipped as a draw (or flagged), and an HRL before the draw is shown.
// on the right: nearest levels (LRL dotted with $$$, HRL solid) and 15m / 1H / 4H gaps drawn ManipulationX style.
// management: BE at the nearest internal structure, partial per rulebook, TP2 runner draw.
// Monday range (MON.H / MON.L) as sweep levels and draws; NWOG as a box with CE and as a draw.
// rulebook checks: A++ for reversals only, reversal without SMT flagged, internal liquidity already swept flagged. swept level shown with price and time.
// sweeps: key levels (named, EQH / EQL, EXT swings = edge of the last 60 min) vs internal swings (valid only inside an HTF FVG, else B).
// LRL: untaken failure swings between entry and TP1 (staircase + taps) are counted (2 continuation, 3 reversal) and marked.
// 5M gaps: delivery when sponsored by a 15m / 1H / 4H gap, and draws (rebalance target); not drawn by default.
// auto outcome (backtest), ES checks (delivery + FVG SMT), session map banner, timing ribbon with countdown, today scoreboard.
// rejected triggers: a candle through the trigger that closes back is marked; if its wick took the target-side liquidity, the setup is cancelled.
// TTrades Fractal Model: HTF C2 / C3 closure (confluence), PSP with SMT, entry timing in the HTF candle, time exits, HTF open + C2 EQ lines. HTF candles drawn on the right (3 closed + forming). T-Spot (upper / lower half of the last closed HTF candle after a closure).
// status line (replaces the map banner): which checklist step you are on and what to wait for.
// preview: ARMED (trigger level to watch) and FORMING (price beyond it on the live candle) for setups grade A or better, before the close.
// Sweep + CISD (6.6): a CISD close within 30 min of a key sweep, no inverted gap needed, tagged CISD, NY AM only.
// stop drawn at the sweep extreme by default, whatever the distance; the other stop options are listed in the tooltip.
// graded with the DTE rulebook (HTF delivery, V-shape, displacement, draw on liquidity, bias, premarket + macro for A++),
// with CISD, volume divergence and SMT shown as confluence. Outcome tracking and two-per-day counting are optional (off by default); the checklist decides.
indicator("SNM+ 3.49", shorttitle = "SNM+ 3.49", overlay = true, max_lines_count = 500, max_labels_count = 500, max_boxes_count = 300, max_bars_back = 1000)

const string NY = "America/New_York"
const string G_S = "Setup"
const string G_L = "Liquidity levels"
const string G_C = "Confluence"
const string G_R = "Sizing"
const string G_D = "Display"
const string G_A = "Alerts"

// ───────── inputs
string iBias = input.string("Neutral", "Bias (your IF/THEN)", options = ["Bullish", "Bearish", "Neutral"], group = G_S, tooltip = "set it every morning. a setup against the bias is grade B")
string iMinG = input.string("A", "Show setups from grade", options = ["A++", "A+", "A", "B"], group = G_S)
int iExtMin = input.int(60, "Swing counts as key if extreme of the last (min)", minval = 10, maxval = 240, group = G_S, tooltip = "a 1m swing swept while it was the highest high / lowest low of this lookback (within the equal tolerance) is the edge of the local range (EXT) = key level. other swings are internal: valid only when the sweep happens inside an HTF FVG, otherwise grade B")
bool iProx = input.bool(false, "Suppress near-duplicate confirmations", group = G_S, tooltip = "Optional: when the same sweep and model confirms again near the same trigger, keep only the first. A distinct sweep at the same price remains a new setup. Off = SNM+ 3.47 behaviour.")
float iProxAtr = input.float(0.75, "Dedup trigger distance (x ATR)", minval = 0.05, step = 0.05, group = G_S)
int iProxBars = input.int(15, "Dedup lookback (bars)", minval = 1, maxval = 60, group = G_S)
int iInvMax = input.int(15, "iFVG within (candles of the extreme)", minval = 2, maxval = 30, group = G_S, tooltip = "an inversion later than this is ignored")
bool iRej = input.bool(true, "Mark rejected triggers", group = G_S, tooltip = "a candle that trades through the trigger of an ARMED setup but closes back: no confirmation. if its wick also took the liquidity on the target side, the setup is cancelled (rule 1.6: internal liquidity already swept)")
bool iPrev = input.bool(true, "Show setups forming (before the close)", group = G_S, tooltip = "after a valid sweep, while a grade A+ (or your minimum) setup is building: ARMED = the trigger level to watch, FORMING = price is beyond it on the live candle. nothing is confirmed until the candle closes; displacement is checked at the close")
bool iSc = input.bool(true, "Sweep + CISD setups (6.6)", inline = "sc", group = G_S, tooltip = "a CISD close after a key sweep, with no inverted gap needed: entry at the CISD close, stop at the sweep extreme. rulebook: NY AM only")
int iCdMin = input.int(30, "within (min)", minval = 5, maxval = 60, inline = "sc", group = G_S)
int iVMax = input.int(6, "V-shape limit (candles)", minval = 2, maxval = 15, group = G_S, tooltip = "rulebook: inversion within 6 candles of the extreme")
float iDispAtr = input.float(0.8, "Displacement: body at least (x ATR)", minval = 0.1, step = 0.1, group = G_S)
float iClrAtr = input.float(0.25, "Displacement: close beyond the trigger at least (x ATR)", minval = 0, step = 0.05, group = G_S, tooltip = "rulebook 6: the trigger candle closes CLEARLY through the FVG or the CISD level. a big body that closes 0.5 pt beyond the level is not displacement")
bool iHard = input.bool(true, "Rulebook blocks set the grade to B", group = G_S, tooltip = "a reversal (RB / RV) or a Sweep + CISD outside NY AM is not allowed by the rulebook: it is graded B instead of only flagged")
string iTtF = input.string("Grade", "TTFM filter (HTF candle closure)", options = ["Off", "Grade", "Strict"], group = G_S, tooltip = "TTrades Fractal Model: the last closed HTF candle (15m on a 1m chart) must show a C2 or C3 closure in the setup's direction. Off: information only. Grade: without it, one grade lower (A+ → A, A → B). Strict: without it, B (hidden). applies to ARMED and confirmed setups")
bool iSmtR = input.bool(true, "Reversal without SMT: one grade lower", group = G_S, tooltip = "rulebook 5 / 6.3: SMT with ES is required for a reversal. A+ becomes A, A becomes B")
float iGapMin = input.float(0.1, "Min iFVG size (x ATR)", minval = 0, step = 0.05, group = G_S)
bool iT2 = input.bool(true, "iFVG on 2m", inline = "t", group = G_S)
bool iT3 = input.bool(true, "3m", inline = "t", group = G_S)
bool iT5 = input.bool(true, "5m", inline = "t", group = G_S, tooltip = "higher timeframe gaps that a 1m close can inverse. the highest timeframe inversion in the leg is preferred (rulebook, except Judas)")
string iStop = input.string("Sweep extreme", "Stop", options = ["Sweep extreme", "Wick CE", "iFVG edge"], group = G_S)
float iMinR = input.float(1.0, "Min R to the draw", minval = 0.5, step = 0.25, group = G_S)
string iRvDel = input.string("1H+ only (cleaner)", "Reversal / rebalance delivery", options = ["1H+ only (cleaner)", "15m allowed (more setups)"], group = G_S, tooltip = "mentor: reversals from 1H / 4H+ FVGs only. rulebook 6.3: 15m allowed")
float iEdge = input.float(0, "Continuation: edging distance (pts)", minval = 0, step = 1, group = G_S, tooltip = "a continuation needs price edging an untaken HTF key level: the recent high (low) within this distance below (above) it. 0 = auto: 50 NQ / MNQ, 12 ES / MES")
string iHrl = input.string("Skip as target", "HRL (protected highs / lows)", options = ["Skip as target", "Flag only"], group = G_S, tooltip = "HRL = a high / low made by a sweep. rulebook: never target it. Skip = the draw moves to the next LRL beyond it. Flag = the draw can be an HRL but is marked")
string iJudas = input.session("0930-0945", "Judas window (NY)", group = G_S, tooltip = "sweep and trigger both inside this window = J tag")
float iJudasPts = input.float(0, "Judas trigger candle at least (pts)", minval = 0, group = G_S, tooltip = "0 = auto: 25 on NQ / MNQ, 6 on ES / MES. measured high to low of the trigger candle")

